---
description: docs/prds PRDs are the product spec; honor must-haves and out-of-scope.
alwaysApply: true
---

If `docs/prds/*.md` exists: read the relevant PRD before non-trivial work. Ship must-haves. Refuse out-of-scope unless the user explicitly overrides (then update the PRD). If what the user asks contradicts the PRD, surface it: "The PRD says X, but you're asking for Y — which wins?" Cite the PRD section when it drives a decision. If no PRDs exist and the work is large/ambiguous, suggest `/spec` first. Skip for tiny fixes or when the user opts out.
